This is a plain COPY of the live desktop dotfiles, not a live one -- nothing
here is managed, symlinked, or read by Home Manager. It exists purely as a
version-controlled backup. Editing a file in here does nothing to your actual
running config; edit the real file under ~/.config or ~ instead, then re-copy
here if you want the backup updated.

VOID LINUX: rice/void-linux/ is a separate, self-contained backup of the
experimental Void install (runit/xbps, MangoWC + DankMaterialShell). Nothing
else in this file describes it -- read rice/void-linux/README. Everything
below this paragraph is the Arch daily driver.

STATUS (2026-08-05): compositor migrated from Hyprland to MangoWC, and shell
migrated from kamalen-shell to a MangoWC port of caelestia-shell
(evoziosk/caelestia-shell-mango). config/hypr/ and everything below that's
Hyprland-specific is NO LONGER ACTIVELY USED -- kept as-is for now (not being
re-synced from a live source, since there isn't one) rather than deleted,
purely as a historical reference in case anything needs to be recovered from
it. May be removed from the local working tree in the future if it's
confirmed nothing still depends on it -- that would only drop it from
future checkouts, not from git history; anything already pushed stays in
this repo's history on GitHub permanently regardless, recoverable any time.
Same goes for kamalen-shell: see config/mangoconfigs/README for the current
active setup (mango + caelestia) vs. what's legacy.

Deliberately left out of Phase 7/8 of the Nix migration (see the main
README) -- this is the live matugen-driven theming + Hyprland/quickshell
setup, and Home Manager taking it over declaratively would fight matugen and
the compositor for control of files they actively regenerate.

config/   (now at arch-linux/config/ -- moved there 2026-10-21 so Arch and Void
          each have their own folder)
          copies of ~/.config/{hypr,waybar,kitty,rofi,swaync,wlogout,foot,
          matugen,fastfetch,qt5ct,qt6ct,cava,fish,gtk-3.0,illogical-impulse,
          spicetify,fuzzel,kde-material-you-colors,Kvantum}, plus:
          config/nvim (just init.lua, lazy-lock.json, matugen_colors.lua --
            not the 404M lazy.nvim plugin data dir under ~/.local/share/nvim,
            which is reproducible from the lockfile anyway)
          config/fontconfig (just fonts.conf)
          config/mpv (just mpv.conf)
          config/{chrome-flags.conf,code-flags.conf,darklyrc,dolphinrc,
            kdeglobals,konsolerc} -- loose top-level files, not directories

          The fuzzel/kde-material-you-colors/Kvantum/mpv/KDE-file additions
          were found by reading ~/.config/illogical-impulse/installed_listfile
          (the ii installer's own manifest of every file it touched
          system-wide) and cross-checking what still exists and isn't covered
          above. Most of that manifest is quickshell/ii/* internal paths,
          already confirmed unused (see below) and not worth reading further.

A parallel, non-git local copy of all of this also lives at
~/.config/hyprbackup, kept in sync the same way -- the only difference is it
keeps the real OpenWeather API key (see below) since it never leaves the
machine.

The actual live quickshell config is config/hypr/scripts/quickshell/Shell.qml
(that's what Hyprland's exec-once actually loads). The top-level
~/.config/quickshell directory (which had an "ii"/illogical-impulse module,
plus hypr-overview/whisker/hypr-lens/music) is NOT used -- confirmed inactive
and deliberately left out of this backup.
home/     (now at arch-linux/home/) copies of ~/.p10k.zsh, ~/.gtkrc-2.0, ~/.aliases
boot/     (now at arch-linux/boot/) Plymouth + GRUB theme sources, copied from ~/Downloads/archplys
          (archply1/arch-mac-style = active Plymouth theme, archply2/
          arch-slider-and-glow = the other installed Plymouth theme, fluent =
          the active GRUB theme). plymouthd.conf says which Plymouth theme is
          active (Theme=arch-mac-style); grub-theme-setting.txt is the
          GRUB_THEME line from /etc/default/grub. To actually reinstall
          either: Plymouth themes go in /usr/share/plymouth/themes/<name>/,
          then `sudo plymouth-set-default-theme -R <name>`; GRUB theme goes
          in /usr/share/grub/themes/<name>/, set GRUB_THEME in
          /etc/default/grub, then `sudo grub-mkconfig -o /boot/grub/grub.cfg`.

Known exclusion: config/hypr/scripts/quickshell/calendar/.env had a real
OpenWeather API key in it. Removed from this copy, replaced with
.env.example (a template). The real key stays only in the live,
untracked ~/.config/hypr/scripts/quickshell/calendar/.env. If you ever want
this properly secret-managed instead of sitting in plaintext, it's a good
candidate for the agenix setup in modules/secrets.nix.

Deliberately excluded, checked and rejected as not being config:
~/.config/zsh (that's not rice, it's live runtime data -- your actual shell
history file and compiled completion cache, exactly what shell.nix's
history.path points at), ~/.config/rice-cooker (despite the name, this is
a Chromium/Electron app's cache/profile directory -- Code Cache, GPUCache,
Trust Tokens, Crashpad -- not theme config), and the top-level
~/.config/quickshell (confirmed inactive, see above -- it had real AI/cloud
API integration code for Gemini/OpenAI/Mistral/Google Cloud plus keyring
scripts; checked carefully before deciding to drop it, all of it reads
credentials from the system keyring at runtime rather than storing anything
in plaintext, so its exclusion here is about relevance, not safety).

Nothing hardcoded was found anywhere in this backup.
